# Private runtime data is read explicitly by Redline. Godot must not import it.
# A GM's extracted map is theirs, and an importer would leave a .import file
# beside it naming a file that is deliberately not in Git.
#
# This ignore covers the maps folder rather than the whole of data/, which is
# where it used to sit. Godot's exporter can only include files its filesystem
# knows about, so ignoring all of data/ kept every shipped table — the item
# catalog, the Lifestyle table — out of every exported build. The JSON beside
# this folder has no importer to go wrong.
